  "final": {
    "agentMessage": "From **CA DMV – Service Advisor result for “vehicle registration renewal office”**:\n\n**Renewing at an office instead of online:**\n\n> **Option 1 – Renew online.** \n> *“In most cases, vehicle registration renewal is no longer processed at the DMV office and can be completed quickly and easily online, saving you time and postage.”*\n> Button: **Renew Online**\n> If unable to use simple online application: **assisted virtual renewal service.**\n\nOther non-office alternatives to save time:\n* **Option 2 – DMV Kiosks:** *“DMV Kiosks use touchscreen technology to guide you through renewing your registration. DMV Kiosks are available inside select DMV offices and retail locations during regular business hours.”* Link: **Find a kiosk near you.**\n* **Option 3 – Renew by mail** *“to the address on your renewal letter.”*\n* **Option 4 – Renew by phone** at **1-800-777-0133.**\n* **Option 5 – Business Partners:** *“Vehicle registration renewals, duplicate sticker orders, and title transfers can be completed with DMV, or with DMV business partners and auto clubs. Business partners are authorized to charge a fee for their services.”* Link: **Find a Business Partner Location**\n\n> **Option 6 – In-person / office visit:**\n> *“There are cases that require renewal in person, such as eligibility, restrictions, etc. In these cases, you may schedule an appointment to renew at the DMV office.”*\n\n**How to save time on the office visit – Option 6 offers 2 paths:**\n\n* *“I am ready to visit the office today.”*\n  Button: **Get in Line Now**\n* *“I need an appointment in the future.”*\n  Link: **Make an appointment for registration renewal.**\n\nNote also:\n*“Your current registration card and sticker may be used until your new registration card and sticker are received. Select Check Registration Status for the latest information.”*"
  },
